ty easy victory  and then eventually we get to a spot  where white is able to just take this  bishop here  on e4 he has two rooks he can easily  trade a rook for a bishop and then he  doesn't have to worry about  too many threats right here and then it  just becomes a matter of  not making a huge mistake now magnus  crossing  credit to him never stopping the attack  the rest  of the game a lot of players would just  resign knowing that they are down  essentially a rook  magnus carlson continues to play the  rest of the game  and then at the end what i appreciate  from yon kristoff is he ends on such a  beautiful move  queen to h7 check king down here to  g4 and you have forced the trade here  you could  take with your queen a very easy victory  but he plays  rook 2e4 check and you can obviously see  yes the queen can take and the queen  falls and white's left with the queen  cannot move the king anywhere we can  still protect the queen  and so in this case madness crosston  recognizes he's going to lose the queen  no way to continue resigns in this  position  was pretty devastated that he lost  125 games still incredible to think  about  hopefully you guys enjoyed this video uh  even if you haven't been watching the  norway chess 2020  now at least you know some of the  highlights that are going on thank you  guys so much for watching i'll see you  in the next video

